  "generated_text": "\nGiven $f(x) = \\frac{1 + x}{1 - 3x}$, we find $f(f(x))$ as follows:\n$$f(f(x)) = f\\left(\\frac{1 + x}{1 - 3x}\\right) = \\frac{1 + \\frac{1 + x}{1 - 3x}}{1 - 3 \\cdot \\frac{1 + x}{1 - 3x}} = \\frac{1 + x + 1 - 3x}{1 - 3x - 3 - 3x} = \\frac{2}{-4} = -1.$$\nThus, $f_1(x) = -1$ for all $x$.\n\nTherefore, $f_2(x) = f(f_1(x)) = f(-1) = -1$, and in general, $f_n(x) = -1$ for all $n \\geq 1$.\n\nThus, $f_{1993}(3) = -1$.\n\nSo, the final answer is $\\boxed{-1}$.",
